# Hermes Mobile

<!-- impeccable:product-schema 1 -->

## Platform

android

## Stack

Native Android views, with Java and the Android SDK. This app requires our own Hermes Agent fork at [{{ fork_repository }}]({{ fork_url }}) for single-host multi-profile `/p/{profile}`, run-scoped instructions, live UI editing, universal push, universal sharing, Smart Notes, visual approval diffs, and Brain Studio.

## Users and operating context

People use their own protected Hermes profile to chat, write code, and return to long-running work from a phone or tablet. One single HTTPS server hostname serves all users and profiles under `/p/<profile>`, each isolated in its own profile directory with its own private workspace, provider credentials, and access key—without needing a separate HTTPS hostname per person. A device can hold more than one account, and users on the same server can share notes, tools, widgets, and discussions with one another.

## Product purpose

Resume a conversation, see what happened while away, and act on the work in the same thread. Coding sessions need readable code and diffs, visible tool activity, and approval requests. Artifacts belong to their originating conversation.

People describe what they want in everyday language, by typing or speaking. Hermes can ask a follow-up question in the same conversation. A person can choose a suggested answer or give their own. When Hermes needs permission to act, show the proposed action and its consequences, with the exact technical details available for inspection.

## Capabilities and constraints

The APK speaks to the Hermes API. Sessions, jobs, model inventory and available tools come from the connected runtime. Show the source and scope of each usage metric. An unavailable cost or timing measurement needs an explicit unknown state.

A user can receive a private alert while the app is closed and unlock the owning account before opening its thread. One single HTTPS server hostname serves all users while isolating each person’s profile directory, workspace, credentials, and access key (and allowing controlled sharing of notes, tools, widgets, and discussions on the same server). An agent can propose changes to the workspace in the conversation where the need arises. The user can preview, apply, and undo them.

## Product principles

- Keep the transcript and composer within reach during ongoing work across phones, tablets, rotation and split-screen windows.
- Keep each question and its answer together. A tap on an approval applies only to the request it names.
- Let people edit a dictated message before sending it. Keep the keyboard available when voice input is unavailable.
- Preserve the user's place, drafts and selections across disconnects, window resizes, incoming events and account switches.
- Keep the entire French interface usable with the keyboard visible, TalkBack, larger text and light or dark appearance.
- Make changes to tools, providers, reminders and layouts explicit and observable.
